cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "vxmcp: an MCP server over vxAPI for the vxedge testbed"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Djaafri"
    given-names: "Fouzi"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vxedge/vxmcp"
url: "https://vxedge.dev"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - software-defined-vehicle
  - automotive
  - testbed
  - reproducible-research
abstract: >-
  vxmcp is a Model Context Protocol server, written in Rust, that exposes vxAPI to agent tooling.
  Each tool is a 1:1 wrapper over one vxAPI RPC with no orchestration logic, and every mutating
  tool asks the user to confirm first. It targets MCP specification 2026-07-28.
references:
